WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.580
An elderly woman watches from her living room
window as heavy sheets of rainfall outside.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.260
She rocks back and forth in her chair nervously.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.900
“It’s been raining for days.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.639
The road is washed out.

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:15.839
I can’t get to town.

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:17.750
What am I to do?

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:18.750
What am I to do?”

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.400
she says out loud to herself.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.420
The rocking chair creaks under her weight,
but not as much as it had three days ago,

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.820
before she ran out of food.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.730
“I am so hungry,” the old lady moans.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.530
She glances at the door that leads to her
basement.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.700
“Maybe I can find something to eat down
there.”

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.680
She stands up, her 90-year-old bones creak,
as she slowly shuffles towards the basement

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.680
door.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.440
The empty chair rocks back and forth from
the old woman’s momentum as if someone is

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.140
still sitting in it.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.300
She opens the door and looks into the pitch-black
darkness.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.510
There are no windows down there, the only
light is connected to a drawstring in the

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:00.960
middle of the room.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.470
The old woman slowly makes her way down the
uneven wooden steps.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:10.370
When she reaches the bottom, she reaches out
her wrinkled hand, groping in the darkness

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.740
for the drawstring.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.610
Her hand brushes something, it feels like
sticky yarn.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.750
Then she feels the legs of a spider scurry
up her arm.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.250
The old woman lets out a shriek as her hand
locates the string, and she pulls hard.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.630
The light flickers on.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:29.350
It creates a dim glow, but at least she can
now see what’s in the basement.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:33.850
The string swings back and forth casting a
snake-like shadow on the far wall.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:38.690
The old woman scans the floor for anything
to eat: a leftover tuna can, some pickled

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:42.290
vegetables, a rat, anything will do at this
point.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.330
There is nothing there.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.310
The old woman feels her strength has been
almost completely drained.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.420
She doesn’t know how she’ll make it back
up the stairs.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.550
In desperation, she looks around the basement
one last time.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.340
Her eyes fall on an old rusty saw.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.820
She pauses for a moment.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.760
“I need to eat,” she whispers.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.420
The old woman slowly walks towards the saw.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.230
She picks it up and examines it.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:12.170
“God gave me two hands for a reason,”
she says, her eyes locked on the rusty blade.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:16.720
She places one hand on the wooden workbench
that sits against the wall and grips the saw

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.150
tightly with the other.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.910
The old woman takes a deep breath and brings
the saw down towards her hand…

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.220
“Where are we going?”

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.520
D-94-322 asks the SCP agent driving the car.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.110
“House on Hadley Hill,” the agent responds.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.910
“Well, that doesn’t sound creepy at all.”

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.270
D-94-322 says as he cranes his neck to get
a glimpse of the top of the mountain through

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:38.270
the SUV window.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:43.160
“Why don’t we just play the quiet game
until we get there,” the agent says as he

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.140
focuses on the pothole-riddled back roads
of Mt.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.220
Zion, Georgia.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:52.960
D-94-322 holds on tightly to the handhold
above him to keep his body from slamming into

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.730
the door every time they go over a big bump.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:00.709
They continue on for a few more minutes when
a rundown house comes into view.

00:03:00.709 --> 00:03:03.120
The agent pulls off the road and stops the
SUV.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.850
“Here you go,” he says, handing D-94-322
an earpiece.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:09.620
“What am I supposed to do with this?”

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.080
D-94-322 asks.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.430
“Just stick it in your ear,” the agent
says with just a little contempt in his voice.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:20.680
“You don’t have to be rude about it,”
D-94-322 replies as he grabs the earbud and

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.170
sticks it in his ear.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.959
“Hello, testing, anybody out there?”

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:29.599
“Hello, D-94-322, can you hear me?” says
a voice in his head.

00:03:29.599 --> 00:03:34.140
“Uhh, yeah, you can just call me D94 for
short.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.310
D-94-322 is kinda a mouthful.”

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.010
“Very well,” the voice from the earbud
agrees.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.220
“My name is Dr. Andrews.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.270
I will be walking you through this test with
SCP-4173.”

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:48.530
“Alright Doc, shall we get this party started?”

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.380
D94 says as he steps out of the SUV.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.840
He looks up at the house that sits atop Hadley
Hill.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.620
The sky is dark, and clouds race over the
mountain as if they would rather be anywhere

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:00.760
else but here.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.090
“Here we go.”

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.709
D94 starts walking up the slippery hill, being
careful not to fall.

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:10.110
He reaches the overgrown walkway leading up
to the house and pauses.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:12.070
“Is there a problem?”

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:13.519
Dr. Andrews asks.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:18.959
“No, just trying to psych myself up to go
into this creepy house,” responds D94.

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:20.719
“What’s inside anyways?”

00:04:20.719 --> 00:04:23.599
“That’s not your concern at the moment.

00:04:23.599 --> 00:04:27.629
But if you do exactly as I tell you, you should
be in and out in no time.”

00:04:27.629 --> 00:04:30.919
“Whatever you say Doc.”

00:04:30.919 --> 00:04:36.970
D94 walks down the path, reaches his hand
out, and grips the cool brass knob.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.159
He turns it and pushes the door open.

00:04:39.159 --> 00:04:42.310
The inside of the house smells like mothballs
and decay.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.020
“Alright, I’m in,” he says

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.410
“Good.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.460
Head down the hallway and turn to your left.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.680
You’ll see a door that leads to the basement.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.819
Let me know when you’re there.”

00:04:51.819 --> 00:04:56.229
D94 walks down the hallway, the old wooden
floor groans under his feet.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:59.850
He reaches the basement door; it is slightly
ajar.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.800
“This place gives me the creeps.”

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.270
“Rightfully so,” Dr. Andrews chimes in.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:08.710
“It is an old spooky house on top of an
old spooky hill in the middle of nowhere.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:11.379
Obviously, it is going to be creepy.

00:05:11.379 --> 00:05:15.879
An old woman died here under mysterious circumstances
around 20 years ago.

00:05:15.879 --> 00:05:18.379
But you don’t really need to worry about
that.

00:05:18.379 --> 00:05:19.689
No ghosts here…

00:05:19.689 --> 00:05:21.009
I think.”

00:05:21.009 --> 00:05:22.330
“You think?”

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:26.559
D94 shouts as he takes a step away from the
basement door.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.520
“I’m just kidding.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:32.620
There’s nothing but harmless old SCP-4173
in that house.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.349
And when has an SCP ever hurt anyone, right?”

00:05:35.349 --> 00:05:38.220
There is a long uncomfortable pause.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:44.349
“Anyways, why don’t you head on downstairs
so we can get you out of there as soon as

00:05:44.349 --> 00:05:45.349
possible!”

00:05:45.349 --> 00:05:49.240
“Yeah, sure,” D94 says as he begins his
descent into the darkness.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.629
“I can’t see anything.

00:05:50.629 --> 00:05:51.740
Is there a light?”

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.669
“No, I think it burnt out years ago.

00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:55.599
But that’s okay; I can guide you.

00:05:55.599 --> 00:05:58.319
It’s what I’m here for,” says Dr. Andrews.

00:05:58.319 --> 00:06:03.069
“Walk towards the east wall, but watch your
head; the ceiling is low in that corner.

00:06:03.069 --> 00:06:05.190
You'll see what you’re looking for when
you get there.”

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:07.219
D94 is silent for a moment.

00:06:07.219 --> 00:06:08.529
“East?” he asks.

00:06:08.529 --> 00:06:10.699
“Turn left,” Dr. Andrews responds.

00:06:10.699 --> 00:06:13.919
“Oh, alright, why didn’t you say so Doc?”

00:06:13.919 --> 00:06:16.599
D94 turns to the left and walks forward.

00:06:16.599 --> 00:06:20.599
After a few feet, there is a loud bang as
he slams his head into the ceiling.

00:06:20.599 --> 00:06:22.249
“Son of a—”

00:06:22.249 --> 00:06:24.789
“I told you to watch your head.”

00:06:24.789 --> 00:06:29.749
“Yeah, thanks,” says D94 as he rubs the
bump forming beneath his hair.

00:06:29.749 --> 00:06:33.229
“This place is even spookier than the first
floor; you know that, right?”

00:06:33.229 --> 00:06:37.710
“I promise there is nothing in that room
right now that can hurt you,” Dr. Andrews

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.370
reassures D94.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.219
“Wait, what do you mean right now?”

00:06:42.219 --> 00:06:44.039
“Don’t worry about it.

00:06:44.039 --> 00:06:47.089
Just let me know when you reach the wall D94.”

00:06:47.089 --> 00:06:50.379
After a few seconds, D94’s eyes adjust to
the darkness.

00:06:50.379 --> 00:06:54.020
He can just make out the damp concrete wall
in front of him.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.089
It looks as if the wall is perspiring.

00:06:56.089 --> 00:06:58.589
“I’m here,” he says.

00:06:58.589 --> 00:06:59.589
“Good.

00:06:59.589 --> 00:07:02.129
There's a little door, maybe five feet to
your left.

00:07:02.129 --> 00:07:04.759
You see it?” asks Dr. Andrews.

00:07:04.759 --> 00:07:05.960
D94 turns.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:07.840
“Yeah, I see it.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:08.840
It's closed.”

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:12.999
The door itself is not very big, maybe a foot
long and half a foot wide.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.999
“Open it,” says Dr. Andrew.

00:07:15.999 --> 00:07:17.199
D94 hesitates.

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:18.660
“What’s in there?”

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.949
“Nothing, just open it,” Dr. Andrews repeats
himself.

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:23.110
“No way man.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:26.429
You’re lying, and I’m not opening anything
until you tell me what’s on the other side

00:07:26.429 --> 00:07:27.429
of that door.”

00:07:27.429 --> 00:07:29.059
Dr. Andrews sighs.

00:07:29.059 --> 00:07:33.580
“We both know that you’re going to do
as I say D-94-322.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.240
You have no other choice.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:39.330
Unless you want to go back to that death row
cell block where we found you.”

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:44.960
D94 shakes his head and rubs the bridge of
his nose.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.580
“Fine,” he says.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:51.639
Dr. Andrews can hear the squeaking of hinges
through the microphone on the D94’s earbud.

00:07:51.639 --> 00:07:53.199
“It’s open; now what?”

00:07:53.199 --> 00:07:54.849
“Do you see anything?”

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:56.169
“Um, no.

00:07:56.169 --> 00:08:01.039
There are some cobwebs and dirt, but other
than that, it’s just dark.”

00:08:01.039 --> 00:08:02.659
D94 thinks for a moment.

00:08:02.659 --> 00:08:04.499
“Why is this little door here?

00:08:04.499 --> 00:08:07.060
Is this some pet door or something?

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:08.060
You'd have to be…

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:10.419
I dunno, pretty small to get in there.”

00:08:10.419 --> 00:08:11.419
“Agreed.

00:08:11.419 --> 00:08:13.520
Just hang tight, and let me know when you
hear something.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:14.929
We won't keep you there long.”

00:08:14.929 --> 00:08:16.020
“Hear something?

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:18.059
Like what?” asks D94.

00:08:18.059 --> 00:08:21.149
“You’ll know when you hear it,” says
Dr. Andrews.

00:08:21.149 --> 00:08:23.610
5 minutes go by without a sound.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:24.729
Then 10.

00:08:24.729 --> 00:08:25.729
15.

00:08:25.729 --> 00:08:28.149
The basement is damp and cold.

00:08:28.149 --> 00:08:32.460
D94 thinks he sees creatures scurrying around
the floor, but he doesn’t say anything because

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:37.370
acknowledging them makes his situation more
real, and a lot more scary.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:40.120
After a half-hour of waiting in silence, D94
screams.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.630
“What the heck was that?”

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:42.700
“What was what?”

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:46.250
Dr. Andrews is startled out of a daydream
by the shouts of D94 in his ear.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.320
“Something just moved past the door!

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.320
I definitely saw it.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.140
What in God’s name was that?”

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:51.260
yells D94.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:55.170
Dr. Andrews tries to remain calm, but he can
barely contain his excitement.

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:58.210
“The entity in the wall is why you're down
there.”

00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:59.540
“What do you mean?

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.600
You said there wasn’t anything down here!”

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.040
“I said there was nothing down there that
could hurt you.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:08.500
If you follow my instructions, this will continue
to be true.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.500
Can you hear anything?” asks Dr. Andrews.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:16.210
“No I can’t hear any—” but before
D94 can finish his sentence, a voice speaks

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.860
from behind the wall.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:21.650
He can’t understand what the voice is saying
at first, but as his heart begins to slow

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:26.300
and the blood stops thumping in his ears,
D94 can make out her words.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.970
“Oh thank goodness.

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:31.390
I wasn't sure you'd be able to find me.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:34.760
What took you so long?” says the voice of
an old woman.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.190
D94 takes a step back from the door.

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:40.770
“There’s someone on the other side of
that wall?” he hisses into the microphone

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:41.770
at Dr. Andrews.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:46.970
“Tell it that the road is out, and you had
to find another way up,” says Dr. Andrews

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:48.160
in D94’s earpiece.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.160
“What?

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:50.160
Why?”

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.610
“Just do it if you want to get out of there,
D94.”

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.910
Dr. Andrews says a little impatiently.

00:09:54.910 --> 00:10:01.960
“Uh, the road is out; I had to find another
way up,” says D94 to the little open door

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:02.960
in the wall.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.090
“Oh yes, the rain washed it out.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:10.470
I was worried I wouldn't ever get to see another
person again, being stuck up here and all.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.800
Can you see me?” asks the voice.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:16.730
“Um, no, I can’t,” says D94.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:19.430
“Doc, what is on the other side of that
wall?”

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:24.480
“Come over here a little closer; I can't
see you properly either,” says the voice.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:26.910
“It's fine; you can get closer.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:29.920
Just don't touch the door,” Dr. Andrews
says.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.610
“I really don’t want to do that,” says
D94.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:36.440
“Do it, and you will be that much closer
to getting out.”

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.350
“I hate you,” whispers D94.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:42.680
He slowly approaches the little door and speaks
into it.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:43.680
“Hello?”

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.450
“Oh, there you are.”

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:48.890
The voice pauses as if whoever is speaking
is examining D94.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.780
“I'm sorry, I can't see like I used to.

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:55.410
It's so dark in here, and it's been so long.

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:59.650
Reach through the door and let me feel your
hand, so I can tell you're really there.”

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:00.650
“What?”

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:02.410
D94 steps away from the door.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:04.620
“No way am I putting my hand in there.”

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.260
“Come now, don't be rude.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:08.810
I just want to feel that you're there.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:10.560
It's been so long.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:13.680
Just a touch,” the voice says a little harsher
than before.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:14.700
“Screw you, lady!

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:19.550
I'm not getting my hands anywhere near this
creepy hole in the wall,” says D94.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:23.280
He turns around and starts walking away from
the little door towards the staircase leading

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.850
back to the main level of the house.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:30.260
Before he can put his foot on the first step,
D94 hears Dr. Andrew’s voice screaming in

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:31.260
his ear.

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.260
“Stop moving!

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:34.600
Look, you're going to have to do it.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:38.210
We haven't been able to recover anyone who
refuses to do what she asks.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:43.650
I can't guarantee your safety unless you put
your hand through that door.”

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.520
“Are you kidding me?”

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:46.520
shouts D94.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:50.730
“You’re telling me that sweet, creepy,
old lady will somehow kill me if I don’t

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:51.730
do as she asks?”

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:56.950
“We’re not entirely sure what happens,
but you need to put your hand through that

00:11:56.950 --> 00:12:00.510
door if you want to get out of there,” says
Dr. Andrews.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:04.150
D94 turns back toward the little door and
slowly approaches it.

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:07.970
“This is my nightmare,” he says more to
himself than anyone else.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:11.160
He reaches out slowly and puts his fingers
through the doorway.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:14.120
He immediately pulls them back and steps away
from the door.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:17.750
“I really don’t want to do this,” D94
whispers.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:21.270
He steps forward again and sticks his hand
all the way through the doorway.

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:23.570
For a moment, nothing happens.

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.600
“Alright, I've got my hand in there.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:26.600
Now what?”

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.660
“Oh, I can see you now.

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:29.880
You're right there.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:30.880
Thank you for coming.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:35.410
It has been so long since someone came, and
with a gift as well?

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:37.010
Sweetling, you're so kind.

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:40.050
So kind to me.”

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.360
“Gift?

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.360
What gift?”

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.810
D94 asks nervously.

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:49.860
“It's so dark and lonesome, and I've just
been so hungry for such a long time.

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.240
Thank you sweetling.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:53.140
I'll take your gift from you.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:57.220
You are such a rude little brat, you don't
really deserve it.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:00.110
You've had it for too long, and you don't
deserve it.

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:01.680
It's mine now.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.310
Mine for my belly.

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:04.310
Thank you.”

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:06.980
“What are you talking about, you psycho?”

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:08.080
D94 stutters.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:11.420
Suddenly, something grabs his hand and pulls
him against the wall.

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:16.400
He screams in agony as Dr. Andrews hears a
wet ripping sound coming through the microphone.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.740
It sounds as if some type of metal instrument
is cutting through flesh.

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:21.020
“Oh, God!

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.020
No!

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:23.020
Help me!

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.230
Help me!”

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.510
D94 screams.

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:26.510
“Please!

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:27.510
Please!

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:31.930
Ple—” Dr. Andrews hears the sound of D94’s
body hitting the floor as he passes out.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.540
It is quiet for a moment.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:36.070
“Don't worry, you ungrateful child.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:37.370
Don't worry.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.370
I'll fill you up too.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:41.060
You can have mine.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:42.260
I'll give it to you.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.460
Sweet boy.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:44.460
Good boy.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.040
Fill you up,” says the old woman’s voice
from the other side of the wall.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:52.600
Dr. Andrews listens as the hinges of the little
door squeak, and it clicks shut.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.590
He picks up the phone next to him and dials
it.

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:55.590
“Go in and get him.

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:58.280
Bring him back to Site-94 for observation.

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:00.940
And try to keep this one alive, please.”

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:05.510
He hangs up the phone and prepares the lab
for D-94-322 to be brought in.

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:11.370
D94 slowly comes out of his medically induced
coma two days after the incident with SCP-4173.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:17.529
He is stable but doesn’t feel great, and
he can’t help but sense that something is

00:14:17.529 --> 00:14:18.529
different.

00:14:18.529 --> 00:14:19.529
He brings his arm up to scratch his face but
feels nothing.

00:14:19.529 --> 00:14:21.180
D94 looks at where his hand should be.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.580
There is nothing there.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:26.060
“That crazy old lady ate my hand!” he
starts screaming.

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:30.370
A medical team rushes in as red lights begin
to flash and sirens blare.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.720
They attempt to restrain D94.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:36.600
During the struggle, D94 catches a glimpse
of himself in a mirror on the far side of

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:37.600
the room.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:39.220
He stops fighting for a moment.

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:41.520
There is a growth expanding from his head.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:46.260
“What the heck is that?” he yells, pointing
to his reflection.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:49.650
D94 begins to struggle again, this time much
more intensely.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:53.450
He begins scratching at the growth on the
side of his head without much success.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:57.170
In the process, he pushes the growth further
into his skull.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.870
It penetrates his brain.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.630
D94 blacks out.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:04.460
The medical team ties D94 to the bed and tries
to get a reading on his vitals.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.160
The growth is putting too much pressure on
his brain.

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:12.420
They rush him to the ER, but D-94-322 dies
before he reaches the operating table.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:16.020
Dr. Andrews stands over the body of the deceased
Class-D subject.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:19.800
“Cut him open,” he says to the doctors
standing in the room.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:23.590
One of them pulls out a scalpel and makes
an incision into the side of D94’s head.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:24.800
“What is that?”

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.470
one of the doctors says.

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:28.480
The other bends over to get a better look.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:31.920
After a moment he turns away and vomits into
his face mask.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:35.370
Dr. Andrews picks up a pair of forceps off
the table.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:40.390
He sticks them deep into the hole in the side
of D94’s head and clamps down hard.

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:43.510
Dr. Andrews pulls out a decomposing hand.

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:47.360
The fingers are still moving as if trying
to grab onto something.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:52.960
There is no explanation for how it got in
there, but it is obvious that SCP-4173 played

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:55.339
some sort of role in the phenomena.

00:15:55.339 --> 00:16:01.790
Dr. Andrews goes back to his office to review
previous case files on SCP-4173.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:06.740
Everyone who has put their hand into the small
doorway has been pulled towards the wall and

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:08.420
had their hand chopped off.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:13.560
The severed appendage never ends up being
a clean-cut, which leads Dr. Andrews to hypothesize

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:18.540
the gruesome makeshift operation is done with
some sort of tool with teeth.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:24.279
Once the hand of the victim is severed, SCP-4173
always thanks the person for their gift.

00:16:24.279 --> 00:16:28.560
She then informs them not to worry about their
hand as it will be replaced.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:31.240
But then something incredibly strange happens.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:36.589
Like with D94, a decaying hand will appear
somewhere in the body, but it isn’t always

00:16:36.589 --> 00:16:38.130
inside the head.

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:42.520
In fact, depending on how polite the test
subject is to the old woman behind the door,

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:46.220
the closer to the wrist the decaying hand
actually ends up.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:50.940
For the test subjects who are rude to the
old lady, the decaying hand ends up in some

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.080
pretty interesting places.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:58.589
“She really hated D-94-322,” chuckles
Dr. Andrews to himself.

00:16:58.589 --> 00:17:03.960
Dr. Andrews continues flipping to the back
of the file on SCP-4173.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:08.829
The SCP Foundation doesn’t quite know how
it happens, but people who refuse to offer

00:17:08.829 --> 00:17:15.140
their hand to SCP-4173 suffer a worse fate
than those who surrender to the old lady.

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:19.569
In every case where a subject tries to get
away from the small door, some inexplicable

00:17:19.569 --> 00:17:24.079
force seems to grab them from behind and drag
them through the tiny opening.

00:17:24.079 --> 00:17:28.799
In these cases, there is nothing left of the
test subject It is likely fatal as a human

00:17:28.799 --> 00:17:33.220
is much smaller than the opening itself, so
the only way a body could fit through the

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:38.720
doorway is if every bone is broken and every
muscle compressed to a quarter of its actual

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:39.720
size.

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:45.309
“I’m not sure which is worse,” Dr. Andrews
says aloud as he closes the file on SCP-4173.

00:17:45.309 --> 00:17:50.369
He glances at the picture paperclipped to
the front of the manila folder depicting the

00:17:50.369 --> 00:17:51.369
tiny doorway.

00:17:51.369 --> 00:17:56.790
He can’t quite pinpoint why, but the fact
that the door slowly closes after the old

00:17:56.790 --> 00:18:01.369
woman gets what she needs from her victims
sends chills down his spine.

00:18:01.369 --> 00:18:05.420
The words of the old woman echo in his head:
“Don't worry.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.690
I'll fill you up too.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.720
You can have mine.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:11.789
I'll give it to you.

00:18:11.789 --> 00:18:12.789
Sweet boy.

00:18:12.789 --> 00:18:14.080
Good boy.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.169
Fill you up.”

00:18:16.169 --> 00:18:23.950
Now go check out “SCP-2696 Haunted Victorian
Mansion” and “SCP-1461 - House of the

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:26.539
Worm” for more frightening anomalous locations!

